  "body": "The following code shows `FOCUS` log twice.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<pre></pre>\r\n<dialog>\r\n  <input autofocus onfocus=\"log()\">\r\n  <a href=\"http://www.google.com/\">Help</a>\r\n</dialog>\r\n\r\n<script>\r\nfunction log() {\r\n  document.querySelector('pre').textContent += 'FOCUS\\n';\r\n}\r\n\r\ndocument.querySelector('dialog').show();\r\ndocument.activeElement.blur();\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\n1. The HTML parser inserts the `input` to the document tree, and it posts the autofocus task.\r\n1. `dialog.show()` sets focus on the `input` synchronously.\r\n1. When the task is executed, the `input` is focused again.\r\n\r\n",
